Z||000000||Gokart||08-17-2000||06:32 AM||||An 88 coupe was just towed into one of the boneyards I deliver to yesterday. Two questions 1) Did all 88's come with a sway bar or was it a buyer option 2) Will these sway bars fit on any year Fiero or are they just interchangeable onto other 88's? Tia for replies <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||08-17-2000||08:56 AM||||88 GT's and Formula's came with rear sway bars; Coupes did not.<P>I'm not positive, but I don't see how the 88 sway bar could fit the 84-87 because the suspensions are so different.||||reg||1
Z||000002||trigger||08-17-2000||09:27 AM||||I don't think the 88 would work since they redid the whole suspension.  If you find a rear swaybar for an 88 and it doesn't work let me know.  Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||08-17-2000||03:56 PM||||'88 sway bars will only fit '88s, so it won't work on your '87.<P>I have a rear '88 sway bar for sale....I just posted it on eBay last night (in case anyone is interested).<BR> ||||reg||10
